To add a Gaussian filter before applying the Sobel operator, you can create a Gaussian kernel with a specific standard deviation (sigma) and convolve it with the grayscale image using the `filter2` function in MATLAB. Here's how you can modify the previous code to achieve this:

```matlab
% Load input image
input_image = imread('image.jpg');
% Convert to grayscale
gray_image = rgb2gray(input_image);
% Define Gaussian kernel with sigma=1
gaussian_kernel = fspecial('gaussian', [5 5], 1);
% Apply Gaussian filter to grayscale image
filtered_image = filter2(gray_image, gaussian_kernel, 'replicate');
% Define Sobel operators in x and y directions
sobel_x = [-1 0 1; -2 0 2; -1 0 1];
sobel_y = [-1 -2 -1; 0 0 0; 1 2 1];
